<title>USA: United States Enrichment Corp Q1 net rises.</title>
<headline>United States Enrichment Corp Q1 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>BETHESDA, Md. 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>(millions)</p>
<p>					   Three Months</p>
<p>					  1996	  1995</p>
<p>Revenue				$422.9	$227.2</p>
<p>Cost of sales			 307.9	 139.9</p>
<p>Gross profit			  115.0	  87.3</p>
<p>Other operating expenses:</p>
<p> Project develop.costs(a)	  35.7	  13.6</p>
<p> SG&amp;A				     8.6	  10.2</p>
<p> Other (income) and expense, net (2.3)	 (0.5)</p>
<p>    Net income (b)		  $73.0	 $64.0</p>
<p>(a)  Project development costs primarily represent research and development spending for the future commercialization of AVLIS uranium enrichment technology.</p>
<p>(b)  As a U.S. government corporation, USEC is exempt from federal, state and local income taxes.</p>
<p>NOTE: It said the significant increase in revenue was attributable to the timing of customer nuclear reactor fuel requirements.</p>
</text>
